  "content": {
    "id": "p108-q71-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Consider the line $4x-3y=14$ and the circle $x^2+y^2-4x-6y+4=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p108-q71-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the line is tangential to the circle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p108-q71-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The line is tangential, with contact point ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(\\frac{22}{5},\\frac{6}{5}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p108-q71-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitution gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "25x^2-220x+484=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", whose discriminant is zero, so there is exactly one intersection.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Substitute the line equation into the circle:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{4x-14}{3}\\\\x^2+\\left(\\frac{4x-14}{3}\\right)^2-4x-6\\left(\\frac{4x-14}{3}\\right)+4&=0\\\\9x^2+(4x-14)^2-36x-18(4x-14)+36&=0\\\\25x^2-220x+484&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe discriminant is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-220)^2-4(25)(484)\\\\\\Delta&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThere is one repeated real root. Each value of $x$ gives exactly one value of $y$ on the line, so the line and circle have exactly one common point. Hence the line is tangential.\nThe contact point is obtained from\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{220}{2(25)}\\\\x&=\\frac{22}{5}\\\\y&=\\frac{4\\left(\\frac{22}{5}\\right)-14}{3}\\\\y&=\\frac65.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p108-q71-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p108-q71-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find the equation of the ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "other",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " tangent to the circle that has the same gradient.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p108-q71-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "4x-3y=-16",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p108-q71-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write the parallel line as ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "4x-3y=k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Substitution and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\Delta=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " give ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=14",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " or ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=-16",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; select the other tangent.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Lines with the same gradient have the form\n$$\\begin{align*}4x-3y&=k\\\\y&=\\frac{4x-k}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the circle and clear the denominators:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\left(\\frac{4x-k}{3}\\right)^2-4x-6\\left(\\frac{4x-k}{3}\\right)+4&=0\\\\9x^2+(4x-k)^2-36x-18(4x-k)+36&=0\\\\25x^2-(8k+108)x+k^2+18k+36&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nEach real root gives one intersection. A tangent has exactly one intersection, so the quadratic must have a repeated root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(8k+108)^2-4(25)(k^2+18k+36)\\\\\\Delta&=-36k^2-72k+8064\\\\\\Delta&=-36(k-14)(k+16).\\end{align*}$$\nFor tangency, $\\Delta=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-36(k-14)(k+16)&=0\\\\k&=14\\text{ or }-16.\\end{align*}$$\nThe given tangent has $k=14$, so the other tangent is\n$$4x-3y=-16.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 110
      }
    ]
